# lowpoly-chain-explainer fix log

## epoch 0 (2026-11-18): created from a reference reel
Made by Claude from the rea-video breakdown of references/ref2.mp4 (56.7 s code-rendered low-poly 3D explainer, one continuous scene, TTS male voice at about 3.3 words/s over a 123 BPM bed, no sound effects), see reference-lab/runs/ref2/analysis-claude (survey + review by Claude) and reference-lab/runs/ref2/crops.
What was taken from the reference:
- Look: near-black violet-tinted ground (L 0.17, C 0.01), thin perspective floor grid, faceted pale grey mountain ring with a fog band at the horizon, flat-shaded neutral grey low-poly models with no outlines; colour only in a thin annotation layer of three hues about a third of the wheel apart (measured: data L 0.86 C 0.10, primary L 0.68 C 0.17 at +145 deg, secondary L 0.70 C 0.15 at -115 deg) plus one payoff hue; a translucent sweep wedge passes about every 1.2 s (the tool's 20 regular "cuts" are this sweep, not cuts).
- Structure: a chain of "If you X, you get Y" sentences, each Y a newly named thing that becomes the next X; overlays accumulate on one scene; a header collects one piece per named thing; a catch at the end; a rewind back to the opening frame, last line ending mid-sentence.
Engine limits met on the way (not changed, the other session owns the engine):
- Captions: the reference's are unboxed, left-aligned at x 90, y about 1400, with the new term highlighted in colour per word; the engine draws a centred boxed caption at y 1600 with no keyword colour. Template works around it: palette.accent = the keyword hue (caption bar), and every new term also gets an on-screen tag.
- One continuous take: the engine adds a cut smear at every shot start; template asks each shot to open on the previous shot's last composition.
- Narrator am_michael (male like the reference) has no measured words/second in the engine (default 2.7), so the length may drift.
Train brief: "Types of missiles: Ballistic Missiles, Cruise Missiles, Hypersonic Missiles".

## epoch 1 (2026-11-18): fixes after reviewing the epoch-0 reel (reels/missiles-chain-e1-v2, $0.242, 47.6 s for 45 s, 551 s wall)
Epoch 0 got the world mostly right (dark violet ground, faceted grey mountain ring with fog, flat-shaded grey low-poly missiles with no outlines, a translucent sweep every few seconds, thin coloured traces, tags, an inset circle and a diagram plate) and a rewind ending. Flaws seen -> fix:
- Chain grammar inverted: the kind was named in the "If you" part and "you get" gave filler ("If you launch a ballistic missile, you get powered flight followed by unpowered ballistic travel") -> strict grammar: the named thing is always the last words after "you get", with a wrong/right pattern (no topic words); per-beat line shapes.
- A "flight_path_scenery" asset (launch slab, terrain shelves, a peak) sat in the middle of every shot -> assets are models only, never terrain/platform/scenery; for a family of kinds one asset per kind (replaces the single hero with a "variant" param); kit.bg: nothing stands in the world.
- Header different in every shot ("B • • •", "S H", "CLASS VEHICLE PROPULSION", "HYPERSONIC FLIGHT CONTROL", "B·C·H·AIR") and 4 shots shipped failing "text spills out of the panel" (vertically) plus empty header plates (the "reserved empty slots" rule) -> header = single letters decided once in the payoff idea, each idea states which letters show; exact plate geometry (y 220, 120 tall, text at y 280, plate width = full header); no plate until the first letter; tags get exact plate geometry too.
- Floor grid nearly invisible, bottom third an empty dark field; mountains up to the frame's middle -> grid 30 to 40% opacity to the bottom edge with a concrete line-spacing formula; horizon y 440 to 500; mountains at most 180 px.
Grading (rea-video decompose of the reel + compare.py) was stopped by Claude Code for low system memory; not rerun.

## epoch 2 (2026-11-18): fixes after reviewing the epoch-1 reel (reels/missiles-chain-e2-v2, $0.239, 42.4 s for 45 s, 958 s wall)
Epoch 1 fixed the chain grammar (every line ends "you get a [kind]": ballistic missile, cruise missile, hypersonic glide vehicle), one model asset per kind and no scenery asset, a clearly visible sliding grid floor to the bottom edge, a consistent sweep wedge, tags in the annotation hues, a side-by-side payoff and a rewind that lands on the first model. Flaws seen -> fix:
- No mountains: kit.bg drew them as thin slivers (bad triangle maths), so the horizon read as a flat grey band and the sky was empty -> concrete peak geometry (apex, base width from height, light left face / dark right face split, 10 to 14 peaks in two rows); "nothing stands in the world" now explicitly excludes the mountain ring.
- Header still not cumulative ("B", then "C" alone, then "HG·V", then "B C H", "B.C.H"), no plate under it; 5 rejections for an empty header plate (earlier letters animated in with k, so the plate showed before its text) -> the header keeps every letter named so far, earlier letters fully shown from the first frame, only the new letter pops in.
- Hypersonic model a lumpy boulder, drawn huge, three models overlapping in a pile (shots 3, 4) -> outlines of long straight edges, never rock-like; the named model 450 to 650 px, earlier models shrink to 260 to 380 px in an upper and a lower lane.
- Tags off the frame edge ("Hypersonic Glide Vehicle" at x 5; 6 rejections, shots 3 and 4 shipped failing) -> tag plate clamped inside x 80 to 1000, at most 14 characters, on the side with more room.
- Link 4 named a description ("hypersonic flight") -> the real other sub-kind by name, or drop the beat (6 shots).

## epoch 3 review (2026-11-18): the epoch-2 reel (reels/missiles-chain-e3-v2, $0.192, 39.2 s for 45 s, 544 s wall); fixes not yet written (3-round limit reached, waiting for go-ahead)
Epoch 2 got the header cumulative (B, then B·C·H held through the twist, payoff and boost-glide shots, back to B at the end), one big named model per shot with earlier models smaller, models no longer piled up, tags mostly inside the frame, a dense side-by-side payoff (traces, nodes, reticle brackets, inset), a rewind with the double-arrow icon that lands on the ballistic missile with its tag. Flaws still seen:
- Mountains still missing: kit.js draws a 12-peak, two-row ring after the sky (a mock-canvas dry run of kit.bg runs clean, 128 fills) but no peaks show in the rendered frames, only the glow and fog band. Cause not found yet.
- Header has no plate in any shot; shot 2 shows only "B" (the C never appears); shot 3 jumps straight to B·C·H.
- Shot 6 tag "hypersonic glide" in 80 px text runs off the right edge (shipped failing after 3 tries); shot 7 shipped with an empty-plate failure.
- Order and facts: the payoff (shot 5) comes before a link (shot 6), and shots 4 and 6 name the same thing twice ("hypersonic glide vehicle", then "boost-glide vehicle").
- Hypersonic model a long flat box; the cruise model is the best of the three.
- 39.2 s for a 45 s target: am_michael speaks faster than the engine's 2.7 words/s default, so the budgeted lines run short.

## epoch 3 fixes (2026-11-18): after the user's review of the epoch-2 reel + the review above
User: "each thing alone in its own frame", "side by side comparisons as boxes, each in its own spot", "very little information: range, impact, speed written there", "everything is cluttered". Changes (template largely rewritten):
- One thing per frame: the previous model flies out, the next glides in; never two models on stage except in the comparison. Accumulating annotations dropped; insets, diagram plates, reticles, flags, regions removed; the sweep cut to 8 to 12% every 4 s. A fixed layout every shot: header (y 200 to 304), a card of numbers (y 340 to 700), the model (centre y 1020 to 1120, 560 to 720 px), its name tag (y 1250), nothing below y 1400.
- Information: every named thing gets a card of 3 real numbers with units, the SAME 3 quantities for every thing (the ones that differ most), written in each shot idea; the twist's card holds the problem's numbers.
- Comparison (payoff): one box per thing stacked down the frame, identical inner layout (name, model on the left, the same 3 rows on the right at the same positions).
- Mountains missing in epochs 1 and 2: rendering the epoch-2 kit's background alone in the stage showed no peaks; cause: the stage's h.rng(seed) returns a generator FUNCTION and the kit used it as a number, so every peak height was NaN. No header plate: the kit called h.rr(ctx, ...) but h.rr / h.poly take no ctx. The template's look section now states both helper signatures (the engine prompts do not).
- Horizon lowered to y 760 to 800 so the sky holds the header and card and the floor holds the model.
- Lines 15 to 17 words (epoch 2 ran 39 s for 45: am_michael is faster than the engine's default rate).

## epoch 4 (2026-11-18): fixes after reviewing the epoch-3-fixes reel (reels/missiles-chain-e4-v2, $0.171, 45.4 s for 45, 507 s wall), not yet run
The rewrite worked: one missile per frame (the previous flies out, the next glides in), a card of numbers on every shot (RANGE 10,000 KM / SPEED MACH 20 ...), the comparison as stacked boxes with identical layout, mountains back on the horizon (h.rng note fixed it), the header on a plate and cumulative (B, B·C, B·C·H), length on target. Flaws seen -> fix:
- Third card row a word, not a number ("MOTION BALLISTIC", "POWERED", "FLIGHT HYPERSONIC"); the hypersonic card used other quantities, and its comparison box other labels (MANEUVER SIGNIFICANT, POWERED BRIEFLY) -> values must start with digits; same 3 labels in the same order for every thing and in every box.
- The comparison had a 4th box for the twist's problem ("PLASMA WAKE") and the header took a 4th letter (B·C·H·P) -> boxes and letters only for the things named in the hook and link shots.
- An extra link after the comparison repeated the cruise missile; the payoff line was vague ("you get one clear distinction") -> N + 3 shots in a fixed order (hook, links, twist, payoff, loop); the takeaway must be concrete and true.
- The hook's first frame showed an empty header plate and "B · ·" placeholder dots -> the header (plate and letter together) only from the naming word.
